Take a failed initial CCR off ims_charging's active_ro_sessions.

An initial CCR bumps active_ro_sessions when it is sent, but the Ro session
only goes into the session table when the CCA grants credit
(link_ro_session() in resume_on_initial_ccr()). Taking it off the count is
done when the session is unlinked, and unlinking a session that was never
linked returns early. So a CCA that refuses the credit (Result-Code 4012, a
call with no credit left), a CCR that times out or a CCA that cannot be used
left the gauge one higher for good, and it kept rising for as long as such
calls were placed. A mix of 60 calls that included 10 without credit left
the gauge 10 higher with no call up.

Take the session off the count in the failure path, where the increment is
known not to have been balanced; the line that did it was commented out.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_charging/ims_ro.c b/src/modules/ims_charging/ims_ro.c
index 652d12cfb7..880aa1e64f 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_charging/ims_ro.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_charging/ims_ro.c
@@ -1770,7 +1770,11 @@ error0:
 
 	LM_DBG("Trying to reserve credit on initial INVITE failed on cdp "
 		   "callback\n");
-	//    counter_add(ims_charging_cnts_h.active_ro_sessions, -1); /*we bumped active on the original initial ccr sent */
+	/* active_ro_sessions was bumped when the initial CCR went out, but the
+	 * session is only linked into the table on a granted CCA, and unlinking
+	 * is what takes it off the count again: a session that never got linked
+	 * has to be taken off here */
+	counter_add(ims_charging_cnts_h.active_ro_sessions, -1);
 	counter_inc(
 			ims_charging_cnts_h
 					.failed_initial_ccrs); /* drop by one as theoretically this is failed initial ccr */
